From: Dan <dan@awto.au>
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: rtl83xx: RTL930x storm control defaults + loop detection (#111)

- Probe: per-port ingress meters on every user port, pps mode: broadcast 10000, multicast 20000
  (all), unknown unicast 20000; CPU port BC/MC only; burst 100 ms; BPDU/RMA/Realtek frames bypass.
  Params storm_bc/storm_mc/storm_uc (0 = off). Core shared with U-Boot: rtl930x_storm.h,
  copied by the build from awto-tl-st1008f shared/rtl930x-storm (never edit the copy).
- Loop detection: RLDP trap to CPU; every 1 s a probe (ethertype 0x8899, RLDP proto, boot nonce)
  out of each forwarding bridge port. One back on a forwarding port of the same bridge = loop:
  MAC TX/RX of the higher port off for loop_recover_s (60), dev_warn. Params loop_detect, loop_recover_s.
- Storm EXCEED flags polled each period: dev_warn on start, dev_info on end, seconds per port/type.
- debugfs rtl838x/storm: state + counters; write "<bc> <mc> <uc>", "loop on|off", "unshut".
---
